% Generate `web/src/studio/DebugReportModal.jsx`: the modal shown when the user STOPS a debug
% recording in the editor. It is the same shell as the app's Feedback modal (reuses its
% `feedback-modal`/`modal-*`/`feedback-*` CSS classes), but the recorded session rides along —
% on Send, the backend attaches a compact analysis of the session to the feedback so the
% developer gets the trace with the report. Discard is a two-step, no-accident action: the first
% click only asks to confirm, and only the confirm actually deletes the session logs (otherwise
% they stay on disk). Closing the modal (✕ / overlay click) keeps the logs — neither sent nor
% discarded — so a stray click never destroys a repro.
%
% Imports: `useState` from 'react'; `* as api from '../api.js'`; `dbg from '../debug/recorder.js'`;
% `IconX, IconCheck` from '../components/icons.jsx'. No inline styles — the class names below are
% the contract with web/src/styles.css.

Default-export `DebugReportModal({ session, onClose })`.

State: `message`, `email` (both ''), `busy`, `sent`, `discarded`, `confirmDiscard` (all false),
`err` (null).

`send(e)` (async): `e.preventDefault()`; early-return if `busy || sent || confirmDiscard` — the
`confirmDiscard` guard matters because while the discard prompt shows, the form has no submit
button, so Enter in the lone email field would implicitly submit and must NOT send. Set busy,
clear err, then `await dbg.flushNow()` FIRST (drains any tail re-buffered by a failed stop-flush
before the backend reads the log), then `await api.sendFeedback({ kind: 'bug', message:
message.trim() || 'Debug session (no description provided).', email: email.trim() || null,
debug_session: session })`; on success `setSent(true)`. On throw, `setErr(String(e.message || e))`
and reset busy (leave busy true on success — the modal switches to the sent view).

`discard()` (async): early-return if busy; set busy, clear err, `await
api.discardDebugSession(session)`, `setDiscarded(true)`; on throw setErr + reset busy.

Render a `modal-overlay` (onClick `onClose`) wrapping a `modal feedback-modal` (onClick
stopPropagation). Inside, an `env-head`: an `env-head-text` with `<h3>Send debug report</h3>` and
an `env-sub` "Your debug recording is attached. Add what went wrong and send it straight to the
developer.", plus an `am-close` IconX button (onClick onClose, title/aria-label "Close").

Then one of three states:
- `sent` → a `feedback-sent`: a `feedback-sent-msg` (`<IconCheck />` + "Thanks — your report and
  the debug recording were sent.") and a `modal-actions` with a Close button (onClick onClose).
- else `discarded` → same `feedback-sent` shape, message "Debug session discarded — nothing was
  sent."
- else a `<form className="feedback-body" onSubmit={send}>` containing:
  - a `modal-err` "⚠ {err}" when err;
  - a `dbg-attach` note: "Only what you did after you started recording — your clicks, scrubs, and
    any errors — is attached. Nothing else from your project is sent.";
  - a `modal-field` label "What happened?" wrapping a textarea (rows 5, maxLength 5000, autoFocus,
    value message, placeholder "Describe the bug — what you did, what you expected, and what went
    wrong.");
  - a `modal-field` label "Email " + a `modal-hint` (style marginTop 0) "(optional — so we can
    reply)" wrapping an `<input type="email">` (value email, placeholder "you@example.com");
  - then branch on `confirmDiscard`:
    - true → a `dbg-discard` block: a `dbg-discard-msg` "If you discard, the debug session logs
      will be deleted and **not** sent. This can't be undone." (the "not" is bolded), and a
      `modal-actions` with a `modal-cancel` type=button "Keep logs" (onClick setConfirmDiscard
      false) and a `dbg-discard-go` type=button (onClick discard) reading "Discarding…" while busy
      else "Discard logs". Both disabled while busy.
    - false → a `modal-actions` with a `modal-cancel` type=button "Discard" (onClick
      setConfirmDiscard true) and a type=submit button reading "Sending…" while busy else "Send
      report". Both disabled while busy.
